PROJECT PROPOSAL – FIRST DRAFT
PROJECT TITLE
Student Study Task Tracker
BRIEF DESCRIPTION
The Student Study Task Tracker is a simple application that helps students organize and monitor their school activities and assignments. Users can add, view, update, and delete tasks. The program will also show the number of completed and pending tasks to help students manage their schoolwork.
PROBLEM STATEMENT
Many students struggle to keep track of their assignments, activities, and deadlines. Sometimes, they forget unfinished tasks or have difficulty organizing their schoolwork. This application aims to solve this problem by providing a simple way to record and monitor school tasks.
OUTLINE OF FEATURES
The application will have the following features:
Add Task – Allows users to add a new school task, including its subject, description, and deadline.
View Tasks – Displays all saved tasks.
Update Task – Allows users to edit task information or change its status.
Delete Task – Removes tasks that are no longer needed.
Task Statistics – Shows the total number of tasks, completed tasks, and pending tasks.
Save and Load Data – Saves task information in a JSON file so the data remains available even after closing the program.
DESCRIPTION OF DATA TO BE COLLECTED AND STORED
The application will collect and store the following information:
Task ID – Unique number assigned to each task.
Subject – School subject of the task.
Task Name – Name or description of the assignment.
Deadline – Date when the task is due.
Status – Whether the task is completed or pending.
The data will be stored in a JSON file. Python lists and dictionaries will be used to organize the information. The program will retrieve and update the saved data whenever users make changes.
The stored information will also be used to calculate task statistics, such as the total number of tasks and the number of completed and pending tasks.
